                      "change": "run(inputs) now computes: out = torch.add(x, y, alpha=0.6)  [u = x + 0.6y]; out = torch.lerp(out, _half_like(out), -0.25)  [= 1.25u - 0.125, one kernel instead of mul_+sub_]; return out.clamp_min_(0.0)  [relu, in place on the freshly allocated tensor]. _half_like caches a 0-dim 0.5 constant per (device, dtype) so no per-call allocation or H2D copy happens. Math identity: 1.25*x + 0.75*y - 0.125 == 1.25*(x + 0.6*y) - 0.125 == lerp(x + 0.6*y, 0.5, -0.25). Neither inputs['x'] nor inputs['y'] is written; only the newly allocated add output is mutated in place.",
